  "caption": "Quinn discovered pickleball, called it \"basically gentle tennis\", and played every day. Then came a lob, a backpedal and a very unhappy calf.\n\nPickleball injuries are rising as returning players ramp up faster than their tissues can adapt. Lunges, pivots and backpedalling load the calves, Achilles, elbows and wrists.\n\nWhat can help: warming up with progressive calf raises, building single-leg calf strength off court, turning and running for lobs instead of backpedalling, and starting with two sessions a week, building up over 6 to 8 weeks. Get niggles checked early.\n\nGet it checked if you feel a sudden \"kicked in the ankle\" sensation, or calf or elbow pain lingers.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
